    "problem_statement": "`or_else` method returns function instead of Result instance\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen calling `or_else` on an `Ok` instance, the method returns the function parameter instead of the original `Ok` instance.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom result import Ok, Err\n\ndef square(x):\n    return Ok(x * x)\n\ndef to_error(x):\n    return Err(x)\n\n# This should return Ok(2) but returns the function instead\nresult = Ok(2).or_else(square)\nprint(f\"Expected: Ok(2), Got: {result}\")\nprint(f\"Type: {type(result)}\")\n\n# This causes AttributeError when chaining\ntry:\n    chained = Ok(2).or_else(square).or_else(to_error)\n    print(chained.ok())\nexcept AttributeError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\nExpected behavior: `or_else` should return the original `Ok` instance when called on `Ok`, allowing for proper method chaining."
  }
